                "entry_id": "93f0e883-6c1d-3471-9f32-761c7940b0a7",
                "word": "unisexuality",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eae64401-60cd-3f41-9a58-49a616dd5c97",
                        "entry_id": "93f0e883-6c1d-3471-9f32-761c7940b0a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The property of being unisexual (having characteristics of a single sex); (especially in botany) the property of being imperfect, i.e. having only male (stamina) or female (pistils) reproductive organs in one flower (monoecism) or individual (dioecism)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20626780-46ca-4bb9-beec-469aac1d0acb",
                                "sense_id": "eae64401-60cd-3f41-9a58-49a616dd5c97",
                                "text": "In all cases of hermaphroditism in animals where unisexuality of the individuals is the rule, the doubly sexed organs are always imperfect, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48aabad9-f8cf-44a7-890a-fb8bc08697db",
                                "sense_id": "eae64401-60cd-3f41-9a58-49a616dd5c97",
                                "text": "As pointed out by Allen (1940), most mutations in the sex genes of hermaphroditic species will tend towards unisexuality, whereas most mutations in dioecious species will tend towards hermaphroditism (or monoecism), […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d3affbc-bba4-3fa5-af84-d258875c6863",
                        "entry_id": "93f0e883-6c1d-3471-9f32-761c7940b0a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being unisex (suitable for any sex)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42a26664-20eb-4211-b127-b4d3411be7ca",
                                "sense_id": "6d3affbc-bba4-3fa5-af84-d258875c6863",
                                "text": "It is somewhat jarring to find the name \"Charlie,\" a name usually [applied to men, applied to a woman] […] those oriented toward female equality or unisexuality in names and behavior will silently approve of his apparent broad-mindedness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84ba6c5a-da7d-41f5-b98a-4b035327e961",
                                "sense_id": "6d3affbc-bba4-3fa5-af84-d258875c6863",
                                "text": "One observes the increasing percentage of unisexuality in Igbo onomastics, and it would not be surprising if such unisexuality invades the area of politically suggestive names."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
